1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,520
Same water,
cold AND warm?

2
00:00:04,570 --> 00:00:06,590
Set out three bowls:
cold, lukewarm, warm

3
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:08,540
Left hand in cold, right hand
in warm water for 30 seconds!

4
00:00:08,590 --> 00:00:10,490
Then put both hands
into the lukewarm bowl

5
00:00:10,540 --> 00:00:14,060
Never use hot water!
Warm tap water only

6
00:00:14,110 --> 00:00:15,830
Hands in!

7
00:00:15,880 --> 00:00:20,830
Your hands are getting used to the water…

8
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:22,830
Now both hands to the middle!

9
00:00:22,880 --> 00:00:24,800
Left hand: warm! Right hand: cold!

10
00:00:24,850 --> 00:00:28,370
It's the same water!

11
00:00:28,420 --> 00:00:30,540
Dashed line = the temperature your hand got used to
(your skin's baseline)

12
00:00:30,590 --> 00:00:32,940
In 30 seconds the baseline moves:
left goes down, right goes up

13
00:00:32,990 --> 00:00:35,110
Lukewarm water above the baseline
feels "warm!"

14
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:37,280
Below the baseline
feels "cold!"

15
00:00:37,330 --> 00:00:41,050
Skin feels how much the temperature changed
more than the temperature itself

16
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:45,850
That's why a pool feels cold at first
and soon feels fine!

17
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:48,300
Try it with an adult, using warm tap water

18
00:00:48,350 --> 00:00:51,000
Nose · pencils · water —
how many fooled you?
